  "semantic_no_existing": [
    "prefer composition over inheritance",
    "single responsibility / one reason to change",
    "write clear self-documenting code",
    "keep it simple / avoid over-engineering / YAGNI",
    "don't add abstraction until it's needed (rule of three)",
    "parse don't validate (true dataflow guarantee)",
    "domain invariants / ubiquitous language",
    "meaningful, intention-revealing names (beyond a casing convention)",
    "architecture / layering boundaries defined by MEANING rather than path (e.g. 'domain must not know about HTTP')",
    "dependency inversion / depend on abstractions not concretions",
    "write good comments that explain WHY not WHAT",
    "small, focused pull requests / atomic commits",
    "make illegal states unrepresentable (encode in the type system by hand)",
    "fail fast / validate at the boundary with domain-specific checks",
    "idempotency of handlers / operations",
    "no premature optimization",
    "consistent error taxonomy / typed domain errors (project-specific)",
    "prefer pure functions / isolate side effects",
    "backward-compatible public API changes only",
    "security: authorize every request / no missing access-control check (semantic, not a lint pattern)",
    "logging must not leak PII / secrets (semantic content check)",
    "tests must be deterministic / no flaky reliance on wall-clock or network"
  ]
}
